invariant: INV-39
file: srv_tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-nonblocking server completes on a client Finished that has
  bytes after it in its record, and srv_complete drops them. RFC 9846
  section 5.1 makes that unexpected_message.
  test/tcp_nonblocking_record_end_tests.h seals the Finished again with one
  byte after it and requires that alert.

--- old
    rc = hsr_check_record_end(&r->hs);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
    srv_complete(&r->hs);
--- new
    srv_complete(&r->hs);
